            "text_size": "40,15",
            "txt_align": "start",
            "sub_heading": "",
            "heading": "",
            "text": "<p>In the e-book we'll summarize <strong>everything healthy walking will bring you<\/strong>. We'll show you the most common mistakes and, with simple exercises, you'll try for yourself <strong>how to move naturally and pleasantly<\/strong>.<\/p><p>Just a little practice and soon you too will switch the<br\/>“walking” program in your brain into a new, <strong>healthy and joyful mode<\/strong>.<\/p><h3>Why take an interest in healthy walking?<\/h3><ul><li>You'll ease the strain on your joints<\/li><li>Your muscles are ready to react at any time<\/li><li>You'll give your maximum performance<\/li><li>You can finally use your lungs' full capacity<\/li><li>You'll activate the pelvic floor<\/li><li>Your body will naturally straighten and lighten<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>And above all<\/strong>: Healthy walking will <strong>bring you joy<\/strong> and contribute to your mental well-being.<\/p><p><em>Lukáš Klimpera - Physiotherapist, founder of Ahinsa shoes and author of the e-book<\/em><\/p>",
